problems, exercise sound judgment, and independently resolve technical issues while recognizing when escalation is appropriate. Ability to collaborate effectively within a team environment while also working independently with minimal supervision. Ability to adapt to changing technologies, priorities, and operational needs in a fast-paced environment. Ability to develop and maintain technical documentation, procedures, and knowledge resources. Ability to maintain confidentiality and safeguard sensitive information while complying with university policies and applicable regulations (e.g., FERPA, HIPAA, Title IX, and security awareness requirements). Technical Skills* Experience supporting Windows, MacOS, and mobile device operating systems. Knowledge of desktop, laptop, printer, peripheral, and audiovisual hardware installation, configuration, troubleshooting, and maintenance. Experience supporting classroom technology, conference room technology, multimedia systems, and collaboration platforms such as Microsoft Teams. Experience with endpoint management and device administration tools such as Microsoft Intune, JAMF, or similar platforms. Experience using IT service management and asset management systems to manage incidents, service requests, inventory, and technology assets. Knowledge of Microsoft 365 services, identity and access management, two-factor authentication, and basic account administration. Working knowledge of networking concepts, including TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, wireless networking, VPN connectivity, and remote support technologies. Demonstrated troubleshooting and problem-solving skills across hardware, software, network, audiovisual, and endpoint technologies. Familiarity with software deployment, hardware lifecycle management, inventory control, and technology refresh processes. Understanding of cybersecurity best practices, endpoint security, phishing awareness, and data protection principles. Requisite Experience* Associate degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant work experience. Experience providing technical support in an end-user computing, service desk, desktop support, or information technology environment. Experience supporting Windows, MacOS, mobile devices, and common business applications. Experience using an IT service management system to manage incidents, service requests, and technology assets. Experience supporting classroom technology, audiovisual systems, or event technology is preferred. Experience with IT asset management, inventory control, hardware deployments, or lifecycle management is preferred. Experience working in a higher education or similarly complex customer-focused environment is preferred."
    },
