    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001172817106": {
      "title": "Accompanist (Music)",
      "description": "Accompanist (Music). Webster Dance Department is seeking part time accompanists to work with our ballet instructors on faculty for various classes through the week. Experience in classical music and variations for accompanying college level dance major courses."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001154328206": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Business Analytics (Webster San Antonio Metro)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Business Analytics (Webster San Antonio Metro). The Department of Computer and Information Science (CAIS) at Webster University in St. Louis, Missouri, is recruiting adjunct faculty to teach the following graduate-level, Business Analytic courses, at the University’s San Antonio Campus in Texas: CSDA 5130 Social and Ethical Issues in Analytics CSBU 5300 Database Systems for Business Analytics CSBU 5320 Data Analytics Foundations for Business Analytics CSBU 5340 ERP Systems and Business Transformation CSDA 5310 Data Visualization CSBU 5420 Machine Learning for Business Analytics CSBU 6300 Descriptive Analytics and ERP Integration Practicum The teaching modalities include: In Person Classroom - On Campus Master’s degree in Business Analytics, Computer Science, Information Systems, Business Administration, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution. At least one year of teaching experience at the postsecondary level. Demonstrated experience using or implementing ERP systems, especially SAP S/4HANA. Proficiency in integrated business processes such as Procure-to-Pay, Order-to-Cash, and Plan-to-Produce. Experience in project management and technical leadership responsibilities. Proficiency in data visualization and analysis tools such as Microsoft Excel and Power BI. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to student success and professional growth. Strong organizational skills and ability to provide timely grading and student support."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001146758506": {
      "title": "Criminology & Criminal Justice Adjunct Professor",
      "description": "Criminology & Criminal Justice Adjunct Professor. The Criminology and Criminal Justice program is seeking an adjunct professor to teach one 16-week section per semester of “CRIM 1050: Introduction to Criminology” or “CRIM 1100: Introduction to Criminal Justice.” CRIM 1050 introduces students to dominant criminological perspectives on why people commit crime, and the patterns and trends of several crime types (violence, property crimes, white collar crime, organized crime, etc). Students will study how cultural, historical, political, and geographical factors affect the patterns of how crime unfolds and the prevalence of crime, especially in the U.S. The course emphasizes criminological theory and the adjunct must be comfortable in this area. CRIM 1100, in contrast, focuses on the functions, development, and efficacy of criminal justice institutions in the U.S. Students will learn about the functions and crime-control capacity of institutions such as the police, criminal courts, corrections, parole, probation, and juvenile justice. The course also addresses the impact of these institutions on different social groups, emphasizing the racial, ethnic, socioeconomic, and gendered impacts of the criminal justice system. Both courses also count towards the Social Systems and Human Behaviors of Webster’s Global Citizenship Program. CRIM 1050 also satisfies the Written Communication requirement, while CRIM 1100 satisfies the Oral Communication requirement; assessment activities for these programs will be required. Both courses are offered on-ground as a lecture course. Class sizes vary from 20 – 30 students. Physical Demands Typical office environment. Location Webster Groves Campus. Minimum Qualifications M.A. or Graduate Certificate in Criminology or related discipline (Sociology, Criminal Justice, Justice Studies, etc.). Relevant teaching and professional experience in the field of criminology and criminal justice. Preferred Qualifications Ph.D. or ABD in fields listed above. Candidates who are also capable of teaching related introductory courses on-ground (such as Introduction to Law, Deviance and Social Control, Introduction to Sociology, or Introduction to Women, Gender, and Sexuality Studies). Department Law, Crime, and Social Justice (which houses the Criminology and Criminal Justice Program) M.A. in Criminology or related field with relevant training and expertise to criminology (Sociology, Criminal Justice, Justice Studies, Legal Studies). Functional/Technical Skills* Basic computer skills (Microsoft Office) PowerPoint or comparable presentation tools"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001090403006": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Applied Behavioral Analysis",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Applied Behavioral Analysis. The Department of Teacher Education is seeking qualified candidates who are enthusiastic about teaching for ongoing part-time adjunct instructor positions in Applied Behavior Analysis. Teaching assignments will vary based on departmental needs. Candidates are expected to perform the following essential duties: Maintain current knowledge of the discipline. Present course material in a clear, organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline-e.g., lecture, demonstration, technology. Explain course expectations clearly to students. Adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Adhere to all university safety policies regarding classroom equipment and materials. Grade assigned papers, examinations, or projects in a timely manner so that students may benefit from the feedback. Provide students with individualized help and consultation to meet students’ needs. Meet administrative requirements and deadlines such as those for submitting course syllabi, conducting student course evaluations, and submitting final grades. Use technology as established and communicated by the University to carry out the administrative duties associated with teaching. General qualifications should be appropriate for the level of class being taught, preferably a master's degree or higher in Behavior Analysis, Education, Psychology, or a related field and/or several years' professional experience in a relevant field. The applicant MUST hold BCBA certification or higher. The applicant should have experience and/or training relevant to the content area being taught. A willingness to work collaboratively with faculty, as well as teach and mentor students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures, and academic backgrounds is essential."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001099489806": {
      "title": "Adjunct Nursing Professor",
      "description": "Adjunct Nursing Professor. Seeking an experienced nurse educator who is able to teach MSN students in the nurse educator practicum as well as instructional strategies, and other MSN level courses. DNP or PhD in Nursing"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001098783606": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Accounting",
      "description": "Adjunct - Accounting. The Business Department is recruiting adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate accounting courses at the home campus in St. Louis, MO. This may include such courses as audit and intermediate accounting. Daytime availability is preferred. The candidate has one of the two following qualifications: 1. Master of Science in Accountancy or equivalent. 2. A business-related graduate degree, the Certified Public Accountant license or the Certified Management Accountant certification, and at least three years of relevant professional experience."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001055657006": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Math and Statistics (San Antonio Extended Campus)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Math and Statistics (San Antonio Extended Campus). Master's degree in statistics, mathematics, applied mathematics, or related field with at least 18 credit hours of graduate coursework in the area of teaching responsibility. Experience in teaching mathematics, statistics to graduate students. Classes are in person on campus and must reside in or near the San Antonio area. Master's degree in statistics, mathematics, applied mathematics, or related field with at least 18 credit hours of graduate coursework in the area of teaching responsibility. Experience in teaching mathematics, statistics to graduate students. Classes are in person on campus and must reside in or near the San Antonio area."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001050160006": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor – Audio Aesthetics & Technology",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor – Audio Aesthetics & Technology. The Audio Aesthetics & Technology department in the School of Communications is looking for adjunct instructors - Responsibilities include but are not limited to, teaching 1-3 courses per semester in the subject of, Audio Media with strong communication and interpersonal skills. Commitment to fostering diversity, equity, and inclusion in the classroom. Willingness to engage in ongoing professional development and collaboration with colleagues. Note that this announcement aims to solicit applications in order to identify a pool of adjunct faculty who are qualified to teach undergraduate and/or graduate coursework in various modalities. Teaching assignments vary based on departmental needs. Applicants must possess a BA degree and/or a minimum of five years of professional experience in the relevant industry. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in any or all of the following: Expertise in any or all of the following areas: sound design, audio recording, editing, mixing, Foley artistry, and field recording. Additional teaching experience and a master’s degree will be a significant advantage."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001042615706": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Information Visualization Course, Interactive Digital Media Program",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Information Visualization Course, Interactive Digital Media Program. Webster University in St. Louis is currently seeking an adjunct instructor for the Interactive Digital Media Program in the Media Arts Department to teach an information visualization course. This course focuses on graphically communicating complex data and data-driven storytelling. Applicants must possess a BA degree and/or a minimum of five years of professional experience in the relevant industry. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in graphic design and motion graphics. Additional teaching experience and a master’s degree will be significant advantages. Note that this announcement aims to solicit applications in order to identify a pool of adjunct faculty who are qualified to teach undergraduate and/or graduate coursework in various modalities. Teaching assignments vary based on departmental needs. Applicants must possess a BA degree and/or a minimum of five years of professional experience in the relevant industry. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in graphic design and motion graphics. Additional teaching experience and a master’s degree will be significant advantages."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001041545906": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Community Music School",
      "description": "Adjunct - Community Music School. Instruct students of various ages and skill levels (beginning, intermediate, and/or advanced) on instrument via online or in-person individual 30, 45, or 60-minute lessons; Correspond with parents/guardians; Attend CMS faculty meetings; Encourage students to participate in CMS recitals; May assist with preparation for competitions and/or festivals Teaching observation/video may be required Bachelors; Prior private lesson teaching required"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5001015827706": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Film, Television & Video Production",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Film, Television & Video Production. Webster University in St. Louis is currently seeking an adjunct instructor for the Film, Television, and Video Production Program in the Media Arts Department to teach beginning to intermediate-level film production courses. Applicants must possess a BA degree and/or a minimum of five years of professional experience in the relevant industry. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in any or all of the following: Film and TV Producing, Directing, Cinematography, Editing, Production Design, or Grip and Electric. Additional teaching experience and a master’s degree will be significant advantages. Note that this announcement aims to solicit applications in order to identify a pool of adjunct faculty who are qualified to teach undergraduate and/or graduate coursework in various modalities. Teaching assignments vary based on departmental needs. Applicants must possess a BA degree and/or a minimum of five years of professional experience in the relevant industry of Film, Television and Video Production. Additional teaching experience and a master’s degree will be significant advantages."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000967131906": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor Environmental Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor Environmental Management. Adjunct instructor position for the Masters in Environmental Management program. Teaching will be in person at the Webster Groves, MO campus, in evenings. Masters in Environmental Science, Environmental Management, Environmental Regulations or related field. Knowledge of current statutory, regulatory approaches to environmental management and operations. Understand project management processes and analytical tools to achieve a sustainable outcome to environmental problems."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000989273106": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Mathematics and Statistics",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor for Mathematics and Statistics. The Department of Natural Sciences and Mathematics is seeking adjunct instructors for MATH and STAT courses. These courses may be in person at our Webster Groves campus or online instruction, depending on the scheduling needs of the department. We are particularly interested in individuals with prior teaching experience in Math or Statistics to undergraduate students. Master’s degree in statistics, mathematics, applied mathematics, or related field with at least 18 credit hours of graduate coursework in the area of teaching responsibility. “Equivalent tested experience” (outside of the classroom) can be used in place of the 18 graduate credit hours of coursework."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000963411800": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor for Biological Sciences (Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Exercise Science)",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor for Biological Sciences (Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Exercise Science). This is a CONTINUOUS OPEN ANNOUNCEMENT for the Webster University Biological Sciences Adjunct Instructor Pool. Webster University seeks to maintain a pool of individuals who are qualified and willing to provide instruction for Biology, Chemistry, Physics and Exercise Sciences. Individuals with experience and appropriate credentials in these areas are encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be required to comply with internal academic policies and with external accreditation agencies standards/requirements in order to retain appointment. Essential Job Duties and Responsibilities Adjuncts are hired on a part-time basis to augment the instructional needs that current faculty members are not available to meet. Qualified Instructors will be chosen from the Adjunct Instructor Pool to teach as specific needs arise. Courses may be online or in person. Modality may be in person lecture discussions or laboratory. Qualifications A Master's degree within the discipline (Biology, Chemistry, Physics, ) with a terminal degree highly desired Excellent communication skills Availability for on campus instruction for traditional course delivery Qualifications ( Desired ) Significant applied experience within the professional setting of identified need Prior teaching experience Publication and/or professional experience Experience with online instruction Master's degree within appropriate scientific field (Biology, Chemistry, Physics) or related field from an accredited institution of higher learning. Professional experience in science or a related field. This position is specifically to teach in St Louis, MO"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000959538000": {
      "title": "Adjunct - Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct - Biological Sciences. Webster University seeks adjunct faculty. Qualifications require terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent master's level in subject area or closely related field). Relevant teaching and professional experience which provides an interdisciplinary base of knowledge."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000961204900": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - San Antonio",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - San Antonio. Webster University seeks adjunct faculty at extended campuses across the United States. Qualifications require terminal degree (Ph.D. or equivalent master's level in subject area or closely related field). Relevant teaching and professional experience which provides an interdisciplinary base of knowledge."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000956302700": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Music",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Music. The instructor will be responsible to deliver required meetings per semester, monitor progress of students toward the completion of the instruction and final exam or jury at the end of the semester. Supervision will be under the auspices of the faculty director of the area of study and the Chair of the Department of Music. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: - Develop syllabi appropriate to each course and level of degree instruction. - Provide all course instruction/lessons on the campus of Webster University. - Evaluate and develop weekly progress of students appropriate to course study.- Position is <29 contact hours/week. Part Time. Master of Arts in Music, Master of Music degree, or advanced degree such as D.M.A. or Ph.D. Demonstrated ability as a performer and teacher of Music Minimum three years of successful experience teaching at the University/Professional level"
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000875599406": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Teacher Education",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Teacher Education. Adjunct Faculty - Department of Teacher Education - Applicant Pool Applications will be held in an applicant pool that will be reviewed when a position opens in a given discipline, to fill that position. Applicants will not be notified of their status. Selected applicants will be contacted for an interview after an opening necessitates consulting the pool. Applicants are encouraged to indicate their availability by completing the Adjunct Questionaire. The Department of Teacher Education is seeking qualified candidates who are enthusiastic about teaching for ongoing part-time adjunct instructor positions. Teaching assignments will vary based on departmental needs. Candidates are expected to perform the following essential duties: Maintain current knowledge of the discipline. Present course material in a clear, organized manner using methodologies appropriate to the discipline-e.g., lecture, demonstration, technology. Explain course expectations clearly to students. Adhere to the requirements of the department's curriculum. Adhere to all university safety policies regarding classroom equipment and materials. Grade assigned papers, examinations, or projects in a timely manner so that students may benefit from the feedback. Provide students with individualized help and consultation to meet students’ needs. Meet administrative requirements and deadlines such as those for submitting course syllabi, conducting student course evaluations, and submitting final grades. Use technology as established and communicated by the University to carry out the administrative duties associated with teaching. General qualifications should be appropriate for the level of class being taught, preferably a master's degree or higher in Education or a related field and/or several years' professional experience in a relevant field . The applicant should have experience and/or training relevant to the content area being taught. A willingness to work collaboratively with faculty, as well as teach and mentor students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures, and academic backgrounds is essential."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000871397006": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Pool - Psychology",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Pool - Psychology. The Department of Psychology is seeking qualified candidates who are enthusiastic about teaching for ongoing part-time adjunct instructor positions. Note that this announcement aims to solicit applications in order to identify a pool of adjunct faculty who are qualified to teach undergraduate and/or graduate coursework in various modalities. Teaching assignments vary based on departmental needs. General qualifications should be appropriate for the level of class being taught, typically a Ph.D. in Psychology or related field. An ABD currently enrolled graduate student will be considered in special cases. The applicant should have experience and/or training relevant to the content area(a) being taught. Willingness to work collaboratively with faculty, as well as teach and mentor students from a wide range of disciplines, cultures, and academic backgrounds is essential."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000868289106": {
      "title": "Game Design Production, Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Game Design Production, Adjunct Faculty. Webster University, School of Communications is seeking an adjunct faculty member to teach in the Media Arts Department / Game Design Production course. Experience and teaching success in the area of Game & Game Design. Webster University, School of Communications is seeking an adjunct faculty member to teach in the Media Arts Department / Game Design Production course. Experience and teaching success in the area of Game & Game Design required."
    },
    "https://myjobs.adp.com/websteruniversity/cx/job-details?reqId=5000857329206": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Management",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Management. The Department of Management at Webster University in St. Louis, Missouri, is recruiting adjunct faculty to teach in the Management Department programs. Graduate level courses typically meet one evening per week for nine weeks. Undergrad courses either meet once a week for 8 weeks or during the day (number of days and times vary per course) over 16 weeks. Faculty teaching at the graduate level shall have at least one of the following: A minimum of a terminal degree (as defined by the discipline) in the same or closely related discipline as the course(s) taught. Alternatively, a minimum of a terminal degree (as defined by the discipline) with eighteen (18) or more earned credit hours in the same or closely related discipline as the courses taught. Evidence of tested experience appropriate to the specific teaching assignment."
    }
  },
